---
import Print from '../../layouts/Print.astro';
import * as site from '../../data/site.js';
const { ENTITY, TBD, TEAM, DOMAIN } = site;
const { BOOK_URL } = site;
const book = BOOK_URL.startsWith('/') ? `${DOMAIN}${BOOK_URL}` : BOOK_URL.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
import { REPORTS } from '../../data/reports.js';
const real = REPORTS.filter((r) => !r.example);
---
<Print title="Arcus one-pager" description="Arcus on one page, to print or forward: what it does, who it’s for, and how to try it free." canonical="/make-the-case">
  <style is:global>.pp{gap:12px}.pp h1{font-size:34px}.pp h2{margin-top:2px}.pp ul{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:18px}</style>
  <div class="row"><span class="logo">arcus<i></i></span><span class="small faint">usearcus.ai</span></div>
  <h1>See which spend is paying off, and where the next dollar should go.</h1>
  <p style="font-size:15px">{ENTITY}</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="sl"><span class="lab"><i class="dot p1"></i>Connect</span><b>Every piece of your data, in one place you own.</b><span>About three months, inside your own setup, and you approve each step. Answers land in Slack, email or Sheets.</span></div>
    <div class="sl"><span class="lab"><i class="dot wf"></i>Count</span><b>Whether your marketing worked, against your own numbers.</b><span>Every sale, ticket or sign-up your ad accounts, partners and creators report, counted once. When you need proof, we run ads in some regions and pause them in others, then compare sales.</span></div>
    <div class="sl"><span class="lab"><i class="dot p3"></i>Listen</span><b>To your audience, everywhere they talk.</b><span>Reddit, TikTok, YouTube, Discord, Twitch, Kick, Goodreads, Fable and more, counted and lined up with your own data.</span></div>
    <div class="sl"><span class="lab"><i class="dot nx"></i>Learn</span><b>What works, and what to make next.</b><span>A few slides with the answer on top, ending in what to keep, test and stop.</span></div>
  </div>
  <h2>Real questions, real answers (names removed)</h2>
  <ul>{real.map((r) => <li><span class="fig">{r.headline.n}</span> {r.headline.label} ({r.kind.toLowerCase()}, {r.who.toLowerCase()}).</li>)}</ul>
  <div class="grid">
    <div><h2>What it costs</h2><ul><li>Try it free: $0, plus a 30-minute walkthrough</li><li>Setup, about three months: {TBD.setup}</li><li>Monthly answers, reports and listening: {TBD.monthly}</li></ul></div>
    <div><h2>What we need to start</h2><ul><li>One question you want answered</li><li>Access to the accounts it touches, like your own sales, tickets or sign-ups</li></ul></div>
  </div>
  <p class="small faint"><b>Team:</b> {TEAM.map((t) => `${t.name}, ${t.title}`).join(' · ')}</p>
  <div class="cta"><b>Try it out for free:</b> usearcus.ai/free-report · Book a call: {book}</div>
</Print>
